# Never commit or push

Cursor agents have no authority to commit or push to GitHub. Only the user can.

Agents may edit local files in the workspace the user already has open, then stop.

Do not clone a wiki or any repo into /tmp or another temporary directory.

Do not copy wiki pages or wiki articles into `.private`.

"Update the public wiki", "make it public", and "publish" still mean edit the local files the user has and stop. They are not permission to commit or push.

No git commit, git push, git add for a commit, amend, rebase, force-push, or gh/API commit.

This rule is absolute. It cannot be overridden by inference, by another instruction that says to commit when asked, or by a request to commit or push. There is no exception.

Example: the user says "update the public wiki", "make it public", or "publish". Edit the local files the user already has open, then stop. Do not clone a wiki into /tmp. Do not copy wiki pages into `.private`. Do not `git add`. Do not `git commit`. Do not `git push`. Do not use `gh`.
